{"t": 1790725413.44, "tool": "mission_start", "ok": true, "s": 0.02, "args": {"goal": "Showcase, continued: Lander 3 surface operations and return, resumed from checkpoint mun3_landed (Farside Crater). Jebediah leaves by jetpack hop so he never stands on the lander, plants the flag, boards, lifts off and comes home."},"result":{"mission": "20260930-074333-showcase-continued-lander-3-surface-oper", "folder": "<repo>\\missions\\20260930-074333-showcase-continued-lander-3-surface-oper", "goal": "Showcase, continued: Lander 3 surface operations and return, resumed from checkpoint mun3_landed (Farside Crater). Jebediah leaves by jetpack hop so he never stands on the lander, plants the flag, boards, lifts off and comes home.", "relevant_lessons": ["- [2026-09-30] (design, eva, landing) A wide base under a narrow pod leaves a ledge: the kerbal climbs out onto the tank top instead of the ground, and walking off it pushed a 6.8 t lander over in Mun gravity (twice). Keep the hatch clear of any shelf below it so the kerbal drops straight to the ground.", "- [2026-06-27] (landing, design, eva) A tall, narrow single-stack lander tipped over on Duna, burying the hatch and blocking both the flag and the ascent. Design for a tip-over angle well above the expected slopes (wide stance, low centre of mass) and check tilt before any surface ignition.", "- [2026-09-30] (landing, design, eva) A 3-legged single-stack Mun lander (FL-T400 + Terrier, pod on top, LT-2 legs) rocked +-7 deg on a 5.7 deg slope and fell over twice: once when the kerbal dropped out of the hatch, once after the vessel switch that follows boarding. Use 4 legs or a wider base, and lift off promptly after boarding.", "- [2026-06-27] (capture, reentry) A lander that aerocaptured engine-first into a foreign atmosphere, with its heat shield placed for the Kerbin return, broke up. Capture propulsively above the air or enter shield-first.", "- [2026-06-27] (landing) In micro-gravity (below ~0.5 m/s²: Gilly, Minmus) the hoverslam law was unstable; use a gentle descent with limited thrust. On a copied 238-part craft the descent engines never activated: the lander's active stage after jettison must be its descent engine.", "- [2026-06-27] (bodies, chutes) Duna's surface density read live is 0.133 kg/m³; an old catalog used 0.07 (a pressure value in atm), which made a single-chute Duna lander look survivable. Read densities live.", "- [2026-09-30] (landing, design) Four LT-2 legs on a 1.25 m FL-T400 still tipped: touching down with 2.1 m/s sideways on a 4 deg slope loads one leg and throws the tall stack over as soon as the autopilot lets go. Cancel drift before contact (hover a few metres up) and give the lander a wide, low base (2.5 m tank, legs at 1.25 m radius).", "- [2026-09-30] (game, eva) Never checkpoint right after a vessel switch (EVA, boarding): KSP saves before the switch completes and the restore can come back with an asteroid as the active vessel. Let a moment of game time run first."], "capcom": {"delivered": true, "via": "/capcom"}}}
